# CODEOWNERS -- who must review a change before it can merge.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The ruleset on this repository already sets
# `require_code_owner_review: true`. Without a CODEOWNERS file that rule matches
# no path and therefore requires nothing: the protection reads as enabled in the
# settings UI and enforces nothing on any pull request. A rule that is on and
# inert is worse than one that is off, because it is believed.
#
# TEAMS, NEVER INDIVIDUALS. GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull
# request, so naming one person as the owner of a path makes that person unable
# to land a change to it alone -- the protection becomes a block exactly when the
# owner is the one working.

*                          @znasllc-io/human-developers

# The deploy substrate. A defect here surfaces as an outage, not a red test.
/deploy/                   @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/.github/workflows/        @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/.github/CODEOWNERS        @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers

# Product identity: the domain, the engine pin, the registry. Every operational
# file reads this, so a wrong value here misconfigures the whole instance.
/product.env               @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/product.env.example       @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
